  "story": {
    "day": 111,
    "title": "Kaya's Afternoon at Home",
    "sentences": [
      "Kaya felt sick, so she stayed away from school.",
      "She lay all afternoon on the living room sofa.",
      "The rainy weather made her feel lonely.",
      "Mom brought medicine and warm barley tea.",
      "Kaya thought about her report and wished to skate around again.",
      "She got a message, a wrong number, but it was fun.",
      "Kaya sat up, finding an elderly witch book with a tail in the corner.",
      "The book talked about a circus; she felt sorry for it.",
      "She decided to volunteer to battle boredom, not sleep.",
      "Kaya would hold the knife and cut the beef and cream cake.",
      "She smelled the cooking. \"Yeah,\" she thought.",
      "\"I belong here; it made a difference, breaking the rule.\""
    ]
  }
}